# apps/academia — Academia Zephyra (external users: learners B2C, Org Admins B2B)
#
# This file is built DELIBERATELY, variable by variable, NOT copied from
# apps/legacy. A wholesale copy of legacy's env is how apps/backoffice silently
# inherited LEARNER_JWT_SECRET at T-fe-007 — and because .env.local is
# gitignored, no reviewer would ever have seen it. The exclusions at the bottom
# are as load-bearing as the inclusions.

# Convex (auto-generated by npx convex dev) — one shared deployment for all apps
CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:xxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=https://xxx.convex.cloud

# Email — transactional (learner magic-link, seat invites).
# PRIMARY: Resend. Set RESEND_API_KEY and src/lib/mailer/learner.ts sends via
# Resend (SPF/DKIM on the verified domain). EMAIL_FROM must be an address on a
# domain verified in the Resend dashboard.
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxx
EMAIL_FROM=Zephyra <no-reply@zephyraconsultora.com>
#
# FALLBACK (legacy Ferozo SMTP) — used only when RESEND_API_KEY is absent.
EMAIL_USER=tu-cuenta-smtp@example.com
EMAIL_PASSWORD=tu-password-smtp

# Auth — LEARNER ONLY. Distinct JWT signing key for the 'session-learner'
# cookie. This is the app that legitimately needs it. It FAILS CLOSED in
# production: src/features/auth-learner/lib/session.ts throws on the first
# sign/verify when NODE_ENV=production and this is unset (resolution is lazy so
# `next build` does not crash). Generate via: openssl rand -hex 32
LEARNER_JWT_SECRET=replace-with-32-byte-hex-string

# App — THIS APP'S OWN ABSOLUTE ORIGIN. REQUIRED; there is no fallback (M4).
#
# Post-split academia is served from academia.zephyraconsultora.com. This one
# variable drives every URL this app generates: the learner magic link
# (/cursos/auth/verify), the org-signup verification link
# (/empresa/registro/crear), the seat-invite claim link (/empresa/invitacion) and
# the SEO/OpenGraph origin of /cursos and /cursos/[slug].
#
# It is read through requireOrigin() from @zephyra/utils, which THROWS when unset
# instead of falling back to the apex. That fallback used to exist and was a
# footgun: the M6 301 map covers only /cursos/:path* and /admin/:path*
# (boundaries v1.1 §3.1), so an apex link to /empresa/* would 404 for a real
# invited learner, and an apex OG url would hand this app's SEO to a host that
# does not serve /cursos. `next build` fails loudly if the Vercel project omits
# it — by design.
#
# Local dev: academia must be the app on :3000 (Next auto-increments, so start it
# first) or set the port you actually used.
# Production: https://academia.zephyraconsultora.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL was RETIRED at M4. It held the same value as
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL, and two variables carrying one value drift; the SEO
# canonical now reads NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL. Do not reintroduce it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY ABSENT — do not add these here
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SESSION_SECRET
#   Admin session signing key. Belongs to apps/backoffice ONLY. Academia serves
#   EXTERNAL users; it must never be able to mint or verify an admin session.
#   Its presence in this app's env would be the first step of a cross-surface
#   escalation path (PDD §7.5, SDD §6 SC #3, boundaries §4).
#
# MAGIC_LINK_HMAC_KEY / MP_ACCESS_TOKEN / MP_WEBHOOK_SECRET / MP_PUBLIC_KEY /
# ZEPHYRA_ACADEMIA_URL (and its deprecated alias ZEPHYRA_PUBLIC_URL)
#   Read INSIDE Convex actions/httpActions only, where process.env resolves
#   against the DEPLOYMENT's env (npx convex env set), not this file. Listed
#   here for discoverability, not to be set here. ZEPHYRA_ACADEMIA_URL must
#   equal this app's NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL — it is how the backend addresses this
#   app in buyer emails and MercadoPago back_urls (boundaries §5).
